    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_505ec8440d6931660721b4f3c8d428ead3a4491ce98c83a44bfb38cd4a7c9199",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds a conditional dependency chain: an approximate functional equation represents zeta(s)^k by complementary finite Dirichlet polynomials; suppression of its error and mixed term would replace the 2k-th zeta moment by two polynomial mean squares; the classical mean-value theorem then fails when the complementary-length constraint forces a polynomial beyond T; and the long-polynomial framework replaces diagonal coefficient energy by shifted-divisor correlation main terms, leading conditionally to the profile w_k(eta).",
