    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5f029e04895aee27ce307dc9f9cc6456b772351c0e20bd53e32add3674737d09",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The factorization of the conjectural moment constant into a prime-local factor a_k and a residual factor g_k lets the source vary their large-k inputs separately. A finite local-factor representation supports the proved asymptotic log a_k=-k^2 log(2e^gamma log k)+o(k^2), while alternative conjectural growth laws for g_k are inserted into the L^(2k)-to-L-infinity bound and optimized in k, yielding respectively square-root-type and near-linear-over-log maximal-order scales.",
