    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6de1bbaad8f99b2dca6c48a603ee53c937bbcb9445b07cb6d46fccad8ea94a1a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source transports local arithmetic into the long-mean-square profile through an explicit sequence. Principal-character pole data of additive twists define P_k; Ramanujan-sum reindexing turns P_k into the divisor-indexed response f_k; the generating function F_k packages the needed d-sum and factors into universal zeta singularities times an analytic residual H_k^*; the value H_k^*(0,0,0)=a_k identifies its leading local arithmetic constant; and Laurent extraction, rescaling, and residue evaluation carry that constant into M_k and then w_k(eta).",
