    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_db551cd644c531fa58abe6bf9c53c01fbdb4b9b91b11bd424e385c73b55f1608",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source uses exact moment information and auxiliary-parameter invariance as two different consistency tests of its conjectural long-polynomial profile. For k=2, extrapolating the profile past eta=1 makes w_2(eta)>2 and contradicts the known fourth moment when combined with the two-polynomial heuristic; for k=3, within the range where both complementary lengths fall under Conjecture 4, w_3(eta)+w_3(1-eta)=42 removes the arbitrary split and recovers the same conjectural sixth-moment constant throughout that range.",
